# Mesh plan step 12, the learner walk-through: "a pipe with water at 2 m/s" to a checked mesh, as someone with fluid
# mechanics and no CFD would go: Mesh > Which mesh? (a straight pipe, 3-D, pressure drop at the walls, water, 2 m/s, 50 mm)
# -> the block builder's pipe O-grid with the first cell for y+ 50 -> Save and mesh -> checkMesh OK.
budget p95 80 max 800
shell mkdir -p $SB/ws/pipe/system && printf 'FoamFile { version 2.0; format ascii; class dictionary; object controlDict; }\napplication simpleFoam;\nstartTime 0;\nendTime 100;\ndeltaT 1;\nwriteControl timeStep;\nwriteInterval 100;\n' > $SB/ws/pipe/system/controlDict
open $SB/ws/pipe
click nav:mesh
wait-until page Mesh
click mesh-which
wait 5
click mq-shape
wait 3
click text:A straight round pipe
click mq-dims#0
click mq-walls
wait 3
click text:Pressure drop, lift, drag (a few %)
click mq-fluid
wait 3
click text:Water, 20 °C
click mq-U
key A ctrl
enter 2
click mq-L
key A ctrl
enter 0.05
wait 5
assert text Block builder, "Pipe (O-grid)" template, graded to the walls
assert text Re 99,600
screenshot $OUT/1_advice.png
click mq-go
wait 10
assert text Pipe (O-grid)
assert text cells. Makes: inlet, outlet (patch), wall (wall).
screenshot $OUT/2_builder.png
click bk-savemesh
wait-until job running timeout 20
wait-until job finished timeout 300
assert log log.checkMesh Mesh OK.
screenshot $OUT/3_meshed.png
